#: ../../../intro/02_contour_map.rst:22
msgid "2. Create a contour map"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/02_contour_map.rst:24
msgid ""
"This tutorial page covers the basics of creating a figure of the Earth "
"relief, using a remote dataset hosted by GMT, using the method :meth:`pygmt."
"datasets.load_earth_relief`. It will use the :meth:`pygmt.Figure.grdimage`, :"
"meth:`pygmt.Figure.grdcontour`, :meth:`pygmt.Figure.colorbar`, and :meth:"
"`pygmt.Figure.coast` methods for plotting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/02_contour_map.rst:31
msgid ""
"import pygmt\n"
"from pygmt.params import Axis"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/02_contour_map.rst:40
msgid "Loading the Earth relief dataset"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/02_contour_map.rst:42
msgid ""
"The first step is to use :meth:`pygmt.datasets.load_earth_relief`. The "
"``resolution`` parameter sets the resolution of the remote grid file, which "
"will affect the resolution of the plot made later in the tutorial. The "
"``registration`` parameter determines the grid registration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/02_contour_map.rst:47
msgid ""
"This grid region covers the islands of Guam and Rota in the western Pacific "
"Ocean."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/02_contour_map.rst:51
msgid ""
"grid = pygmt.datasets.load_earth_relief(\n"
"    resolution=\"30s\", region=[144.5, 145.5, 13, 14.5], "
"registration=\"gridline\"\n"
")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/02_contour_map.rst:63
msgid "Plotting Earth relief"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/02_contour_map.rst:65
msgid ""
"To plot Earth relief data, the method :meth:`pygmt.Figure.grdimage` can be "
"used to plot a color-coded figure to display the topography and bathymetry "
"in the grid file. The ``grid`` parameter accepts the input grid, which in "
"this case is the remote file downloaded in the previous step. If the "
"``region`` parameter is not set, the region boundaries of the input grid are "
"used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/02_contour_map.rst:71
msgid ""
"The ``cmap`` parameter sets the color palette table (CPT) used for "
"portraying the Earth relief. The :meth:`pygmt.Figure.grdimage` method uses "
"the input grid to relate the Earth relief values to a specific color within "
"the CPT. In this case, the CPT \"oleron\" is used; a full list of CPTs can "
"be found at :gmt-docs:`reference/cpts.html`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/02_contour_map.rst:78
msgid ""
"fig = pygmt.Figure()\n"
"fig.grdimage(grid=grid, frame=Axis(annot=True), projection=\"M10c\", "
"cmap=\"SCM/oleron\")\n"
"fig.show()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/02_contour_map.rst:90
msgid "Adding a colorbar"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/02_contour_map.rst:92
msgid ""
"To show how the plotted colors relate to the Earth relief, a colorbar can be "
"added using the :meth:`pygmt.Figure.colorbar` method."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/02_contour_map.rst:95
msgid ""
"To control the annotation and labels on the colorbar, use the ``annot`` "
"parameter to set the annotation interval (in this case every 1,000 meters), "
"the ``label`` and ``unit`` parameters to set the labels along the long and "
"short dimensions of the colorbar, respectively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/02_contour_map.rst:100
msgid ""
"By default, the CPT for the colorbar is the same as the one set in :meth:"
"`pygmt.Figure.grdimage`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/02_contour_map.rst:105
msgid ""
"fig = pygmt.Figure()\n"
"fig.grdimage(grid=grid, frame=Axis(annot=True), projection=\"M10c\", "
"cmap=\"SCM/oleron\")\n"
"fig.colorbar(annot=1000, label=\"Elevation\", unit=\"m\")\n"
"fig.show()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/02_contour_map.rst:118
msgid "Adding contour lines"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/02_contour_map.rst:120
msgid ""
"To add contour lines to the color-coded figure, the :meth:`pygmt.Figure."
"grdcontour` method is used. The ``frame`` and ``projection`` are already set "
"using :meth:`pygmt.Figure.grdimage` and are not needed again. However, the "
"same input for ``grid`` (in this case, the variable named \"grid\") must be "
"input again. The ``levels`` parameter sets the spacing between adjacent "
"contour lines (in this case, 500 meters). The ``annotation`` parameter "
"annotates the contour lines corresponding to the given interval (in this "
"case, 1,000 meters) with the related values, here elevation or bathymetry. "
"By default, these contour lines are drawn thicker. Optionally, the "
"appearance (thickness, color, style) of the annotated and the not-annotated "
"contour lines can be adjusted (separately) by specifying the desired ``pen``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/02_contour_map.rst:133
msgid ""
"fig = pygmt.Figure()\n"
"fig.grdimage(grid=grid, frame=Axis(annot=True), projection=\"M10c\", "
"cmap=\"SCM/oleron\")\n"
"fig.grdcontour(grid=grid, levels=500, annotation=1000)\n"
"fig.colorbar(annot=1000, label=\"Elevation\", unit=\"m\")\n"
"fig.show()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/02_contour_map.rst:147
msgid "Color in land"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/02_contour_map.rst:149
msgid ""
"To make it clear where the islands are located, the :meth:`pygmt.Figure."
"coast` method can be used to color in the landmasses. The ``land`` is "
"colored in as \"lightgray\", and the ``shorelines`` parameter draws a border "
"around the islands."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/02_contour_map.rst:155
msgid ""
"fig = pygmt.Figure()\n"
"fig.grdimage(grid=grid, frame=Axis(annot=True), projection=\"M10c\", "
"cmap=\"SCM/oleron\")\n"
"fig.grdcontour(grid=grid, levels=500, annotation=1000)\n"
"fig.coast(shorelines=\"2p\", land=\"lightgray\")\n"
"fig.colorbar(annot=1000, label=\"Elevation\", unit=\"m\")\n"
"fig.show()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/02_contour_map.rst:170
msgid "Additional exercises"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/02_contour_map.rst:172
msgid ""
"This is the end of the second tutorial. Here are some additional exercises "
"for the concepts that were discussed:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/02_contour_map.rst:175
msgid ""
"Change the resolution of the grid file to either ``\"01m\"`` (1 arc-minute, "
"a lower resolution) or ``\"15s\"`` (15 arc-seconds, a higher resolution). "
"Note that higher resolution grids will have larger file sizes. Available "
"resolutions can be found at :meth:`pygmt.datasets.load_earth_relief`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/02_contour_map.rst:180
msgid ""
"Create a contour map of the area around Mt. Rainier. A suggestion for the "
"``region`` would be ``[-122, -121, 46.5, 47.5]``. Adjust the :meth:`pygmt."
"Figure.grdcontour` and :meth:`pygmt.Figure.colorbar` settings as needed to "
"make the figure look good."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/02_contour_map.rst:185
msgid ""
"Create a contour map of São Miguel Island in the Azores; a suggested "
"``region`` is ``[-26, -25, 37.5, 38]``. Instead of coloring in ``land``, set "
"``water`` to \"lightblue\" to only display Earth relief information for the "
"land."
msgstr ""

